```
Reason:
These statements assume that the MCP251x CAN controller will enter configuration mode within a fixed time frame after a reset. If the device takes longer than expected to power up, this check can return an error prematurely, even though the device is still initializing.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
timeout = jiffies + HZ;
while ((mcp251x_read_reg(spi, CANSTAT) & CANCTRL_REQOP_MASK) !=
       CANCTRL_REQOP_CONF) {
    usleep_range(MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000,
                 MCP251X_OST_DELAY_MS * 1000 * 2);
    if (time_after(jiffies, timeout)) {
        dev_err(&spi->dev,
            "MCP251x didn't enter in conf mode after reset\n");
        return -EBUSY;
    }
}
```
Reason:
These statements implement a loop that continuously checks if the MCP251x has entered configuration mode, allowing for retries and a longer wait time. This ensures that the function does not give up too early, accommodating boards that require more time to initialize after a reset.

